ors, textures, and edges; then using these features to identify objects in the images. I used a CNN that has already learned the features from a giant dataset of 1.2 million images called ImageNet. There are different types of CNNs that have different structures (architectures) that work better or worse depending on your criteria. With this project you'll explore the three different architectures (AlexNet, VGG, and ResNet).","topics":[],"score":249357,"global_rank":63350},{"name":"rocket3989/ieeextreme14","owner":"rocket3989","html_url":"https://github.com/rocket3989/ieeextreme14","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"CUC Bat Knights' Solutions for ieeextreme 14","topics":[],"score":249353,"global_rank":63361},{"name":"dbrent-amazon/advertising-api-python-report-request","owner":"dbrent-amazon","html_url":"https://github.com/dbrent-amazon/advertising-api-python-report-request","stars":2,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"How to request a report using Python.","topics":[],"score":249351,"global_rank":63366},{"name":"TheNeuralBit/task-gmail-sync","owner":"TheNeuralBit","html_url":"https://github.com/TheNeuralBit/task-gmail-sync","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Python script for synchronizing a gmail label and taskwarrior tasks","topics":[],"score":249350,"global_rank":63367},{"name":"sap2411/python_practice","owner":"sap2411","html_url":"https://github.com/sap2411/python_practice","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":249339,"global_rank":63385},{"name":"micloudon/djangomysql","owner":"micloudon","html_url":"https://github.com/micloudon/djangomysql","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":249339,"global_rank":63388},{"name":"lovincyrus/Metropolis","owner":"lovincyrus","html_url":"https://github.com/lovincyrus/Metropolis","